      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A good point towards this;\nMost things people do with avatars really only needs one audio source playing at a time.\nYou to have walking, jumping, and landing sound effects?\nThat's easily a series of 3 small sound files that you will never really want to have overlap at any given moment.\nIt doesn't need to be 3 separate components taking up 75% of your excellent performance rating.\nAdding a script like this will encourage more interesting and polished avatar designs as creators will feel less pressured not to use sound effects.\nI made a similar post before knowing about this one:\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/multiple-sound-file-audio-source",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-19T22:38:57.949Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Having an officially supported audio bank script would allow creators to add multiple audio clips to one audio source (reducing total audio source count on any given avatar)\nConsidering that having too many audio sources on your avatar will break them, this seems like a viable workaround.\nPerhaps there could be support for animateable \"firing\" of specific audio clips, removing the need to animate audio sources on and off. This could also be used for one-shot sound effects that are meant to play until they end, even if the animation is disabled, ie. Gunshots, etc.",
